@lang en
IMPORT `bvvcx-claim`

-- Both sides of the two caps the settlement tests do not reach: the 10% cap on rescue and
-- towing (10.2.2) and the sum insured (12.4, and BVVC06's own "never above the sum insured").
-- Expected values worked by hand from the source.

§ `Tests — the limits`

§§ `10.2.2: rescue and towing, at most 10% of the sum insured`

GIVEN `the towing` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A claim`
`the standard collision, towed for` `the towing` MEANS
    `a claim: vehicle` `the standard vehicle` `, policy` `the standard policy` `, claimant` `the insured named on the certificate`
        `, event` `the standard collision` `, driving` `the standard driving` `, conduct` `prompt and proper conduct`
        `, shortfall` `no premium shortfall` `, costs` (`costs: at the insurer's request` TRUE `, preventing further damage` 0 `, rescue and towing` `the towing`)
        `, hire` NOTHING `, wreck` `no wreck kept` `, other insurance` EMPTY

-- Under the cap: 16m + 5m. At the cap (60m of a 600m sum insured): 16m + 60m. Over it: still 60m.
#ASSERT `the amount payable on` (`the standard collision, towed for` 5_000_000) EQUALS 21_000_000
#ASSERT `the amount payable on` (`the standard collision, towed for` 60_000_000) EQUALS 76_000_000
#ASSERT `the amount payable on` (`the standard collision, towed for` 60_000_001) EQUALS 76_000_000

§§ `12.4: never above the sum insured`

GIVEN `the clauses` IS A LIST OF `A supplementary clause`
GIVETH A `A claim`
`a 200m repair on a car insured for 100m of its 600m, under clauses` `the clauses` MEANS
    `a standard claim under` (`a 2026 policy with sum insured` 100_000_000 `, deductible` NOTHING `, clauses` `the clauses`) `for` `the event` `,` `the standard driving`
    WHERE
        `the event` MEANS `a sudden` `a collision` `on 15 June 2026, damaging` (LIST (`a part repaired:` "body" `, of kind` `an ordinary part of the vehicle` `, caused by` `the insured event itself` `, for` 200_000_000))

-- 200m is under 75% of 580m: a partial loss. With BVVC06 (no pro-rating): 200m - 0.5m, capped
-- at the 100m sum insured. Without it: 200m x 100/600 - 0.5m = 98,500,000/3, under the cap.
#ASSERT `the amount payable on` (`a 200m repair on a car insured for 100m of its 600m, under clauses` (LIST `BVVC06 (settlement up to the limit of liability)`)) EQUALS 100_000_000
#ASSERT `the amount payable on` (`a 200m repair on a car insured for 100m of its 600m, under clauses` EMPTY) EQUALS (98_500_000 DIVIDED BY 3)
